  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership for improving prospects for forcibly displaced and host communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Second Phase of the MFA&apos;s Partnership with IFC, ILO, UNHCR, UNICEF and the World Bank to improve prospects for forcibly displaced and their host communities by together pushing for a transformation from taking a humanitarian to a development approach towards forced displacement. The 5 partners will push this transformation by focusing on the nexuses between, education, protection, employment, WASH and critical infrastructure. The partnership has been rolled out in 8 countries: Iraq, Jordan, Lebanon, Egypt, Sudan, Ethiopia, Kenya and Uganda. This Activity appraisal document will highlight the second phase of this Partnership and the specific role and activities of the World Bank under this Partnership which will be funded by the MFA. 

Ethiopia ETOL
This activity has been topped up with 20.000.000 USD as it was decided to include a Worldbank project (grant) in Ethiopia. Please see MINBUZA-2025.2536736 (proposal) and MINBUZA-2025.2536748 and MINBUZA-2025.2536745 (mail-track).</narrative>
  </description>
